470 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (As the overseer of the Citizenship by Investment Programme \(CIP\) in Saint Lucia, I am proud to say that our operations have consistently upheld the core governing principles of integrity, efficiency, accountability and transparency. )
/E (As the overseer of the Citizenship by Investment Programme \(CIP\) in Saint Lucia, I am proud to say that our operations have consistently upheld the core governing principles of integrity, efficiency, accountability and transparency. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
471 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Our Board, composed of five seasoned professionals, remains fully committed to fulfilling our mandate to the government and people of Saint Lucia. Sixty-percent of Board members have been accredited through the Director Education and Accreditation Programme Charter governance institute of Canada \(CGIC\) demonstrating our dedication to serving our country with the utmost respect and diligence.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
472 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Integrity)
/E (Integrity)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Integrity lies at the core of all Citizenship by Investment Programs, shaping the ethical foundation and credibility of these initiatives. As the demand for second citizenship through investment continues to rise, the need for upholding integrity within investment migration programs becomes increasingly paramount.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
474 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In the early months of 2022, the investment migration industry faced significant challenges in processing applications for individuals from Russia, Belarus and Iran. Due to the political unrest in these regions, the Citizenship by Investment Unit was unable to conduct proper due diligence and accept funds from applicants within these jurisdictions. As a result, Saint Lucia made the decision in February 2023 to suspend receipt of applications from the above noted countries. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
475 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Additionally, the Citizenship by Investment Unit experienced significant delays in processing bank fees due to limitations with its two banking partners. This led to significant delays in the processing of citizenship applications and agent license applications during the reporting period. A testament to the enhancement and successes of the marketing efforts initiated in the previous reporting period of 2021/2022.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
476 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (As the demand for second citizenship through investment continues to rise, and challenges within the industry persist, the imperative of upholding integrity within the investment migration industry becomes increasingly paramount.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
477 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (02)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
478 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( Annual Report 2022-2023)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
479 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Chairperson, Citizenship by Investment Board)
/E (Chairperson, Citizenship by Investment Board)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
480 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T <43484149524D414E905320464F5245574F5244>
/E <43484149524D414E905320464F5245574F5244>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
481 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Efficiency )
/E (Efficiency )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (One of the key drivers of success in the investment migration industry is the efficiency of application processing times to which Saint Lucia programme was negatively impacted. To address these challenges, the Citizenship by Investment Unit implemented creative and innovative solutions to streamline internal processes. This included setting and achieving targets by departments, improving the marketing of its pre-processing module, and establishing strategic partnerships with key due diligence stakeholders such as the Joint Regional Communication Center \(JRCC\), the Royal Saint Lucia Police Force \(RSLPF\), and reputable third-party Due Diligence firms.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
483 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (As a result of these efforts, the average processing times for citizenship applications during the reporting period of 2022/2023 decreased by an impressive 65% compared to the previous reporting period of 2021/2022. Applications with up to two dependents were processed within 35 business days, while applications with more than two dependents were processed within 63 business days. This significant improvement in processing times not only demonstrates the Citizenship by Investment Unit's commitment to efficiency and excellence but also enhances the overall experience for applicants seeking citizenship through investment.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (We are steadfast in our commitment to effectively manage our Citizenship by Investment Programme. We recognize the dynamic nature of the investment migration market and, therefore, the Board has dedicated itself to actively promoting our investment migration product in various key jurisdictions, including the United States of America, Europe, the Middle East, and Africa. Our efforts extend beyond promoting our investment migration product to also enhancing the reputation of Brand Saint Lucia.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Programme has been significantly improved with the introduction of the VIBE initiative, which urges citizens granted through the programme to Visit, Invest, Build, and Establish themselves in Saint Lucia. This initiative aims to eliminate the transaction barriers that have traditionally existed within the investment migration industry, transforming it into a platform for partnership and growth.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (As part of the enhancements to the Citizenship by Investment Programme, a new investment option has been launched under the Government Bond Option. This option eliminates the temporary and non-viable products that were previously offered. One of the new investment options is the National Action Bond, which has been available for investment starting from 1 January 2023. This non-interest-bearing bond has a minimum investment amount of US $300,000.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (These improvements to the Programme not only streamline the investment process but also provide more sustainable and attractive options for potential investors. Saint Lucia is committed to fostering a conducive environment for investment and growth, and these enhancements are a testament to that commitment.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (03)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( Annual Report 2022-2023)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Chairperson, Citizenship by Investment Board)
/E (Chairperson, Citizenship by Investment Board)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
491 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T <43484149524D414E905320464F5245574F5244>
/E <43484149524D414E905320464F5245574F5244>
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
