492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Accountability)
/E (Accountability)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Accountability in investment migration programs refers to the responsibility of governments and stakeholders to ensure transparency, integrity, and adherence to regulations under such programs. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
494 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Citizenship by Investment Programme was a crucial component of the evaluation process conducted by the Caribbean Financial Action Task Force \(CFATF\) in relation to anti-money laundering measures. Despite not being a reporting entity, the Citizenship by Investment Unit \(CIP Saint Lucia\) has actively engaged and participated in the CFATF monitoring and evaluation process for the past five years.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Accountability mechanisms such as due diligence checks on applicants, third-party audits of investments, and reporting requirements are essential to maintaining the credibility and legitimacy of our programs and we continue to work closely with key stakeholders in the management such.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (As a Board, we have recognized the need for various changes to enhance efficiency and customer service within the investment migration industry, while ensuring the integrity and security of our citizenship by investment programme remains uncompromised. The launch of the VIBE on 1 January 2023, marked a significant milestone, accompanied by legislative changes introduced through the Citizenship by Investment \(Amendment\) \(No. 2\) Regulations.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (These changes include the implementation of a background and due diligence fee of US $7,500 for assessments on all developers seeking approval for CIP Real Estate or Enterprise Projects. Additionally, a new Government Bond option has been established with the introduction of a National Action Bond requiring a minimum investment of US $300,000.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Furthermore, the threshold for Real Estate Investments has been reduced from US $300,000 to US $200,000. Moreover, individuals granted citizenship through the CIP have had the opportunity to include dependents by submitting an application and meeting the required investment criteria through the program. In response to this, the Board has increased the investment amount for newborns \(0-12 months\) from US $500 to US $5,000. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (We understand that accountability is crucial for maintaining trust in investment migration programs and protecting the interests of both investors and our Saint Lucia.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Transparency)
/E (Transparency)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
501 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The promotion of citizenship through investment is a strategic marketing approach designed to attract high-net-worth individuals interested in obtaining citizenship by making a significant financial contribution to a country. This practice involves utilizing the benefits of investment migration programs to appeal to potential investors seeking to enhance their global mobility and access new opportunities. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
502 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (During the reporting period of 2022/2023, the Board initiated efforts to establish strategic partnerships with key global marketing partners; CS Global Partners \(6 June 2022\), Arton Capital \(10 June 2022\), Latitude Consultancy Limited \(20 October 2022\) and Bluemina Citizenship & Residency Inc \(12 January 2023\). These partners have played a crucial role in the strategic marketing and promotion of our investment migration product and further Brand Saint Lucia by helping to enhance our outreach and attract more potential investors and visitors alike.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (04)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( Annual Report 2022-2023)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Chairperson, Citizenship by Investment Board)
/E (Chairperson, Citizenship by Investment Board)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T <43484149524D414E905320464F5245574F5244>
/E <43484149524D414E905320464F5245574F5244>
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
507 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Despite facing numerous challenges, our Saint Lucia program achieved significant success thanks to the dedicated team of professionals at the Citizenship by Investment Unit. In the 2022/2023 reporting period, we saw an impressive 85% increase in citizenship applications compared to the previous year, with a total of one-thousand and seventy-six \(1,076\) citizenship applications received. However, during the period, five-hundred and forty-four \(544\) were granted citizenship, while eight \(8\) applications were denied.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
508 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (This reporting period saw a 12% increase in gross revenue generated through the Citizenship by Investment Programme, totaling EC $60,631,316 in addition to the following remitted to the Government and People of Saint Lucia as per the various investment categories namely, the National Economic Fund \(NEF\) totaling EC $41,371,397 and the Covid-19 Government Bonds totaling EC $42,295,519. These achievements demonstrate the effectiveness and efficiency of our program, and we look forward to continuing to serve our clients and contribute to the growth and development of our Saint Lucia.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
509 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Closing)
/E (Closing)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (As a Board, we are excited to continue collaborating with our key stakeholders to enhance Saint Lucia in 2023 and beyond. We have successfully transformed the Citizenship by Investment Unit and Programme from its humble beginnings to its current status as a leading provider of second citizenship and a welcoming home for individuals. We are committed to further improving our services and offerings to ensure that Saint Lucia remains a top choice for those seeking a second citizenship.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
